<title>USA: Restore income averaging for farmers-US lawmakers.</title>
<headline>Restore income averaging for farmers-US lawmakers.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A handful of U.S. lawmakers announced Thursday they were sponsoring legislation to allow farmers to average their income for income tax purposes.</p>
<p>At a news conference, they said the proposal would cost $90 million over five years but be invaluable for helping farmers cope with fluctuations in income. They denied it would be a tax loophole or impede efforts to balance the budget.</p>
<p>Rep. Nick Smith, R-Mich., said the bill would allow farmers to average income over two years. Companion bills will be filed in the House and Senate, he said, and House leaders were willing to consider the idea.</p>
</text>
